PRETABLE 19 -- written 2026-10-16 BEFORE table 19 runs (its own file; this mtime orders table 19 alone).
Instrument: probe v23 (m88k_exc_probe_v23.FROZEN.py, md5 1d400b64...) = v22 + repair 14, the delay-slot CLASS CLOSURE as
Fable 5.1 enumerated it on pass 14.  It REPLACES the table-18 candidate: that candidate's two frozen rows used br.n +16
inside the handler at 0x40, whose target 0x50 is the ERROR entry, so a lost ERROR delivery would have read DELIVER
(errdslot could not see M_DS865 at all).  Base: HEAD 7b23b785.

THE ENUMERATION (to be VERIFIED by the closing pass, not hunted): the delivery path TESTS PSR & SFRZ (:811) and
cpu->delay_slot (:840, and :865 whose write X(br_n) consumes at cpu_m88k_instr.c:99).  Floor = {7 labels} x {SFRZ} x
{delay_slot} = 28 cells; v22 rows 19; v23 adds 9 -> 28/28:
  (0,1) BOUNDS dslotbounds, ERROR dsloterror           -- unfrozen tb1 in a slot (the trap route is the only route there)
  (1,1) MISALIGN errdslotmisalign, OVF errdslotovf, DIV0 errdslotdiv0, PRIV errdslotpriv, UNIMPL errdslotunimpl,
        BOUNDS trapfrozen7dslot, ERROR trapfrozen10dslot  -- the frozen div0 handler re-faults in a br.n +8 slot
  plus usfu1dslot (the fallback, clause (e) by the tests-not-reads criterion, rowed on its measured escape).
DISCLOSED, clause (e), each measured below as an escape: the trap route at the five instruction labels in a frozen slot
(M_RRDS_<L>); {delay slot} x {a PSR bit other than SFRZ}; three-or-more-axis joints; vectors 0..3 (m88kexchwtraps).

CHANNEL per new row and the mutant it kills (73 fault rows):
  dslotbounds / dsloterror        M_DSNOT_BOUNDS / _ERROR: fallback HALT replaces DELIVER at 0x38 / 0x50
  errdslot<L> (five)              M_DSFRZ_<L> (`implemented = !(delay_slot && (PSR & SFRZ))' at L): HALT replaces DELIVER at 0x50
                                  M_RRNTDS (`!is_trap && !delay_slot'): delivered to L's own vector -> STOP
                                  M_DS865 (`delay_slot && update_shadow_regs' at :865): X(br_n) jumps to the SELF after the
                                  handler -> STOP
  trapfrozen7dslot                M_DSFRZ_BOUNDS: HALT; M_RRTDS (`!is_trap || delay_slot'): re-routed to 0x50 -> STOP; M_DS865: STOP
  trapfrozen10dslot               M_DSFRZ_ERROR: HALT; M_RRTDS: 0x50 WITH the re-route diagnostic -> BADREGS(refatal); M_DS865: STOP
  usfu1dslot                      M_FBDS (`&& !delay_slot' at :799): no halt -> TAILHALT or a delivery, never HALT

